    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d594-a4-a7">

                <pb facs="0578" n="504" xml:id="pg504"/>

                <head>No. 3.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#center">[Official
                            despatch.–Telegram.—<placeName>Corunna</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1865-02-12">February
                    12</date>.]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Perry, American Chargé d’Affaires:</hi></p>
                <p>Pledges were given by the French government to our late minister, Dayton, that
                    the ram should not be transferred to the rebels. Cannot Bigelow, at Paris,
                    obtain the intervention of French with that of Spanish government to arrest the
                    ram now fitting out at Ferrol, or to detain her until her case has been
                    thoroughly investigated.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CRAVEN, <hi rendition="#italic">Commanding the
                    Niagara.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum</hi>—This was answered immediately to the
                        effect that Mr. Bigelow and myself had already done everything which could
                        be done, and that there was no reliance to be placed on anything except his
                        guns.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
